-- title:
--   Level descent of the rigid Γ_{H_1} chart at q=3
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q = 3$, $M'$ a nonzero level with $q \nmid M'$ (hypothesis `hqM'`), and $\ell_g$ a prime with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$ (hypotheses `hℓg`, `hℓg12`, `hℓgM'`). Further data: a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; a finite set $W$ of places of the field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ (the intermediate field generated over the residue field of $A$ by the two $j$-series $j$ and $j(\mathsf q^{M'})$) with a distinguished element $s \in W$; an inclusion $\mathrm{hle}$ of the base change $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ of the level-$M'$ function field to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ into $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M' = \mathrm{xHFunctionFieldBar}\,(q^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M')$; a constant reduction $R_0$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ along $A$ with values in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$, i.e. a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, a surjective residue map with kernel its maximal ideal, a map on places preserving degrees, and the usual compatibilities of a `ConstantReduction`; an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\mathbb{Q}$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with elements $\pi_0$ (lying in $A$, by `hπ`), $\zeta_0$, $\varpi_t$, $\xi$; a natural number $\ell$; an intermediate field $K_b$ of $k_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with a valuation subring $A_b$ of $K_b$ cut out by $A$ (hypothesis `hAb`) and an element $\varpi_b \in A_b$; a subgroup $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^{\times}$ with $H_1 = \mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M' \sqcap \ker\big((\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell_g)^\times\big)$ (hypothesis `hH₁`); an intermediate field $K_\ell$ of $k_0$ in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,k_0$, an algebra over $A \cap k_0 := A.\mathrm{comap}\,(\mathrm{algebraMap}\,k_0\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ compatibly with $k_0$; a nonzero $j_\ell \in K_\ell$; an element $\varpi_t' \in A\cap k_0$ with $\varpi_t' = \varpi_t$ (`hϖt'`); an ideal $y$ of the chart algebra $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,(A\cap k_0)\,K_\ell\,j_\ell$ (the elements of $K_\ell$ integral over the $(A\cap k_0)$-subalgebra generated by $j_\ell$); an $(A\cap k_0)$-subalgebra $B_t$ of $K_\ell$ and a valuation subring $W_t$ of $K_\ell$ with $B_t \subseteq W_t$ (`hBW`); natural numbers $n, m$; $\gamma_0 \in \mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$ and a $k_0$-automorphism $\tau_0$ of $K_\ell$; an element $\zeta_c$ of the completion of $A\cap k_0$ at its maximal ideal; the element $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,k_0\,q$ of $K_\ell$ (`hjK`); an element $a_0 \in A\cap k_0$; and a finite set $\mathrm{ends}$ of subrings of $K_\ell$.
--
--   The hypotheses fall into the following groups. Arithmetic of the reduction: `hA` says $q$ is a nonunit of $A$; `hW` says $W$ consists exactly of the supersingular places $\mathrm{ssPlaces}\,q\,M'$; `hR₀` says that $R_0$ computes the coefficientwise reduction, namely for a Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose image lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ that image is $R_0$-integral and its residue is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Local structure at $q$: `hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres` say that $A\cap k_0$ is a henselian discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal $(\pi_0)$ and algebraically closed residue field, and `hκ` says every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0 \cap A$. Auxiliary constants: `hℓ`, `hℓ3`, `hℓq`, `hℓM'` say $\ell$ is prime, $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \ne q$, $\ell \nmid M'$; `hζ₀` says $\zeta_0$ is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity; `hξ` says $\xi$ is a primitive $q$-th root of unity; `hϖtA` and `hϖt` say $\varpi_t \in A$ and $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q\cdot u$ for a unit $u$ of $A$; `htame` says $\ell_g - 1$ is a unit of $A\cap k_0$; `hKb` says $K_b = \bot$, and `hϖb`, `hϖb0` say that the maximal ideal of $A_b$ is generated by the nonzero element $\varpi_b$. Identification of the level field: `hKℓ` says $K_\ell$ is the $k_0$-base change $\mathrm{laurentBaseChange}\,k_0\,(\mathrm{xHFunctionField}\,(q^2M')\,H_1)$, and `hjℓ` says $j_\ell$ is the image of the $j$-series $\mathrm{jq}$ under coefficient extension.
--
--   The chart point: `hy` and `hϖy` say $y$ is maximal and contains $\pi_0$; `hss` says that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism from the chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the image of the coordinate $j$ lies in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q\,\Omega$, the set of $j$-invariants all of whose elliptic curves are supersingular; `hover` says that $y$ specialises to the place $s$: for every $g$ in the level-$M'$ modular function field which is $R_0$-integral, has poles only where $j$ does (the condition $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}\,j \Rightarrow 0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}\,g$ at all places $P$), whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, and whose image lies in the chart algebra, and for every $c \in k_0$ lying in $A$ whose residue equals the value of that $R_0$-residue at $s$, the difference $g - c$ lies in $y$; `hOrbit` says that every maximal ideal $y'$ of the chart algebra which contains $\pi_0$ and satisfies the same specialisation condition is carried to $y$ by a level automorphism, i.e. there are $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and an automorphism $\tau$ of $K_\ell$ with $\mathrm{IsLevelAutAt}\,k_0\,q\,\xi\,q\,(q^2M')\,H_1\,\gamma^{-1}\,K_\ell\,\tau$ (the condition that $\tau$ implements $\gamma^{-1}$ on $q$-expansions of ratios of modular forms of level $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions, under any embedding of $k_0$ in $\mathbb{C}$ carrying $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$) which preserves the chart algebra and matches $y$ with $y'$. Finally `hjC` and `ha₀y` say that $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,k_0\,q$ lies in the chart algebra and that its difference with $a_0$ lies in $y$.
--
--   The rigid-chart hypotheses, whose clauses are summarised here: `hS1` (a conjunction of thirteen clauses) requires that the chart algebra is contained in $B_t$, that $K_\ell$ is the fraction field of $B_t$, that $B_t$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A\cap k_0$ with $B_t/\pi_0$ of Krull dimension at most $1$, that $W_t$ is a discrete valuation ring over $A\cap k_0$ with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, inducing $y$ on the chart algebra and obtained from $B_t$ by inverting the elements outside its maximal ideal, that for every $(\mathbb{F}_{q^2})$-algebra structure on the residue field $\kappa_0$ of $A\cap k_0$ there is a surjection $\rho \colon B_t \to \mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa_0$ (the Drinfeld coordinate ring $\kappa_0[x_1,x_2]/(\text{Drinfeld polynomial}-1)$) whose vanishing locus is the maximal ideal of $W_t$, which is $\kappa_0$-linear on constants and equivariant for level automorphisms attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ through an element $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, c)$ of $\mathrm{hSubgroup}\,q$ acting by $\mathrm{hAction}$, with $c \ne 1$ for nontrivial $\tau$ coming from $\Gamma(q)$ and with a companion automorphism realising the purely scalar element $(1,c)$, that $B_t$ is stable under all level automorphisms for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, that every prime of $B_t$ containing $\pi_0$ is the pullback of the maximal ideal of $W_t$ along some level automorphism, and that an element of $B_t$ all of whose level translates lie in the maximal ideal of $W_t$ is divisible by $\pi_0$. `hR7` (a conjunction of eleven clauses) requires that $\tau_0$ has exact order $n$ on $B_t$, that every level automorphism preserving $W_t$ acts on $B_t$ as a power of $\tau_0$, that $\mathrm{ends}$ has $q+1$ elements permuted transitively by the level automorphisms preserving $W_t$ and fixed individually by $\tau_0$, that distinct ends are separated by an element which is a nonunit in one and a unit in the other, that the ends are the localisations of one finite-type level-stable subalgebra $B_c$, and that each end $O$ is a local noetherian ring contained in $W_t$ and containing the chart algebra, with residue field that of $A\cap k_0$, whose completion is identified by an isomorphism $\iota$ with the crossing model $\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}$ over the completion of $A\cap k_0$ with parameter $\pi_0^m$ in such a way that two elements $c_x, c_y$ with $c_xc_y = \pi_0^m\cdot(\text{unit})$ correspond to unit multiples of $U$ and $V$, with $c_y$ in and $c_x$ outside the maximal ideal of $W_t$, with $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,k_0\,q - a_0$ a unit multiple of $V^e$ for some $e \ge 1$, with $\tau_0$ corresponding to an automorphism $\theta_0$ scaling $U$ by $\zeta_c$ and $V$ by $\zeta_c^{-1}$ modulo the square of the maximal ideal, together with an Igusa-type discrete valuation subring $W_x$ separating $O$ from the other ends and a level-stable finite-type subalgebra $B_x$ of $B_t\cap O$ with prescribed pole behaviour; the last clause of `hR7` states that a valuation subring of $K_\ell$ over $A\cap k_0$ containing the chart algebra and inducing $y$ either contains $B_t$ or dominates one of the ends. `hR9` requires an element of $B_t$ lying outside every valuation subring over $A\cap k_0$ at which $\pi_0$ is a nonunit and $j_\ell$ is not integral (no monic polynomial over $A\cap k_0$ evaluated at $j_\ell$ is a nonunit), and `hR10` requires, for each maximal ideal $y''$ of the chart algebra containing $\pi_0$ which is not in the level orbit of $y$, an element of $B_t$ lying outside every valuation subring that supports the corresponding translated specialisation.
--
--   The deck-group data: `hn1`, `hnq`, `hn` say $1\le n$, $n \mid q+1$ and $n = 2\,\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s$, where $\mathrm{placeWidthChar}$ is the quotient of $\mathrm{jWidthChar}\,q$ at the value of the geometric $j$-generator at $s$ by the ramification invariant $\mathrm{placeRamificationJ}\,M'\,s$; `hγ₀Γ`, `hγ₀Γ0`, `hτ₀`, `hτ₀W` say that $\gamma_0 \in \Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$, that $\tau_0$ realises $\gamma_0^{-1}$ as a level automorphism, and that $\tau_0$ preserves $W_t$; `hm1`, `hm` say $1\le m$ and $\pi_0^m = \varpi_t'\cdot(\text{unit})$; `hζc`, `hζcprim` say $\zeta_c^n = 1$ and $\zeta_c^k - 1$ is a unit for $0<k<n$. Finally `hInert` requires, for every $(\mathbb{F}_{q^2})$-algebra structure on the residue field of $A\cap k_0$, a map $\rho$ with the four properties listed in `hS1` together with an exponent $\eta \in \{1,q\}$ such that for every $\pi$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$, every compatible pair $(\sigma_L,\sigma_A)$ of ring automorphisms of $k_0$ and of $A\cap k_0$ inducing the identity on the residue field, with $\sigma_A\pi = \alpha_t\pi$ and $\alpha \in \mathbb{F}_{q^2}^{\times}$ lifting the residue of $\alpha_t$, and every ring automorphism $\tau$ of $K_\ell$ acting coefficientwise through $\sigma_L$: $B_t$ and $W_t$ are $\tau$-stable and, for $d \in (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$ with image $\alpha^{q+1}$, the map $\rho$ intertwines $\tau$ with the action of $(\mathrm{diagOneElem}\,q\,(d^{\eta})^{-1}, \alpha^{\eta}) \in \mathrm{hSubgroup}\,q$.
--
--   Conclusion. Give $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ the $k_0$-algebra structure obtained by composing $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$. Then for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $k_0$ in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ consisting exactly of those elements all of whose Laurent coefficients lie in $k_0$, there exists a valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ with the following properties.
--
--   (i) For $x \in k_0$: $x \in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ lies in $W_0$. (ii) $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring. (iii) The image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates its maximal ideal. (iv) For every $g$ in the level-$M'$ modular function field which is $R_0$-integral, has poles only where $j$ does, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$: the image of $g$ in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$, and for every $c \in k_0\cap A$ whose residue in $A$ equals the value at $s$ of that $R_0$-residue, $g - c$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$. (v) $W_0$ is stable under the level automorphisms $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ for every primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta \in \mathrm{Idx}\,q$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, in the sense that for $f \in F_0$ whose image also lies in $F_0$, $f \in W_0$ if and only if its image lies in $W_0$.
--
--   (vi) There exist a subring $B$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ and an $A_b$-algebra structure on $B$ such that: the structure map is the inclusion of $A_b \subseteq K_b \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ into $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$; $B$ is contained in the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_b$, and every element of that compositum is a quotient of two elements of $B$ with nonzero denominator; $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$, and $B/\varpi_b$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$; the image of $\varpi_b$ is a prime element of $B$; $W_0$ consists exactly of the quotients $g/h$ with $g,h \in B$ and $\varpi_b \nmid h$; the image of $\mathrm{jq}$ lies in $B$; $B$ is stable under all $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; there is an element $b$ of $B\cap F_0$ lying outside every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ which is over $A$, has $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal, and at which $j$ is a nonintegral element (no monic polynomial over $k_0$ with $A$-integral coefficients evaluated at $j$ is a nonunit of $V$); and for every $s' \in W$ with $s' \ne s$ there is an element of $B\cap F_0$ lying outside every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ over $A$ which supports the specialisation to $s'$ (the condition of (iv) with $s$ replaced by $s'$ and $W_0$ by $V$).
--
--   Moreover $B$ carries two reduction statements. First, for every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field $\kappa$ of $A$ for which $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa$ is a domain, and every $\zeta \in \mathrm{Idx}\,q$, there are a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho \colon B \to \mathrm{quotField}\,q\,\kappa\,C_s$ (the fixed field in the Drinfeld function field of the scalar actions by $C_s$) such that $\#C_s = 2\,\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s$; $\ker\rho$ is generated by $\varpi_b$; $\rho$ is compatible with $A_b \to \kappa$; every element of $\mathrm{quotField}\,q\,\kappa\,C_s$ is a quotient of elements of the image of $\rho$; the image of $\rho$ consists exactly of those elements whose images in the Drinfeld function field lie in the image of $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa$; and for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, 1) \in \mathrm{hSubgroup}\,q$, $\rho$ intertwines $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma^{-1}$ with $\mathrm{hFunctionFieldAction}$ at that element. Second, for every ring homomorphism $\iota \colon \mathbb{F}_{q^2} \to \kappa$ (taken as the algebra structure) with $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa$ a domain, there is a single $C_s$ of the same cardinality such that for every $\zeta \in \mathrm{Idx}\,q$ there is a $\rho$ with the five properties just listed and, in addition, an exponent $\eta \in \{1,q\}$ such that for every $\pi \in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$, every $\tau$ in the inertia subgroup $A.\mathrm{inertiaSubgroupIn}\,\mathbb{Q}$ stabilising $k_0$, every $\alpha \in \mathbb{F}_{q^2}^\times$ with $\iota(\alpha) = A.\mathrm{tameCharacter}\,\pi\,\tau$, and the semilinear automorphism $g = \mathrm{arithmeticGalois}\,(\mathrm{xHFunctionField}\,(q^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'))\,\tau$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$: $B$ is $g$-stable, and for $d \in (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$ with image $\alpha^{q+1}$ and $(\mathrm{diagOneElem}\,q\,(d^\eta)^{-1}, \alpha^\eta) \in \mathrm{hSubgroup}\,q$, $\rho$ intertwines $g$ with $\mathrm{hFunctionFieldAction}$ at that element.
--
--   Finally, $B$ comes with the node structure at $s$: the image of $\mathrm{jq}$ is $R_0$-integral with residue in the valuation subring of $s$, $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\,q$ lies in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, there is $a_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$ whose residue satisfies $\mathrm{residue}(a_0)^q =$ the value at $s$ of the $R_0$-residue of $j$, and there is a finite set $\mathrm{nodes}$ of subrings of $F_0$ such that: $\mathrm{nodes}$ has $q+1$ elements; there is a subring $B_c$ of $F_0$, generated by the constants from $k_0\cap A$ together with a finite set, contained in every node and such that every node is the set of quotients $g/h$ with $g,h \in B_c$ and $h$ a unit of that node; the level automorphisms attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ permute $\mathrm{nodes}$, and for every $\zeta$ and any two nodes some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ carries the first to the second; distinct nodes are separated by an element which is a nonunit of one and a unit of the other; every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ over $A$ supporting the specialisation to $s$ (the condition of (iv) with $W_0$ replaced by $V$) either contains $B$ or dominates a node (some $O \in \mathrm{nodes}$ with $O \subseteq V$ and nonunits of $O$ landing in the maximal ideal of $V$); and every node $O$ satisfies: $O \subseteq W_0$; $O$ is a local noetherian ring; $x \in A \iff$ the image of $x \in k_0$ lies in $O$; every element of $O$ differs from a constant from $k_0\cap A$ by a nonunit of $O$; and there exist $E_0 \ge 1$, a unit $v$ of $A\cap k_0$ with $\pi_0^{E_0} = \varpi_t^{\,2\,\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s}\cdot v$, elements $c_x,c_y \in O$, a unit $u$ of $O$, an isomorphism $\iota$ from the completion of $O$ at its maximal ideal onto $\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}$ over the completion of $A\cap k_0$ with parameter $\pi_0^{E_0}$, and units $\gamma_U,\gamma_V$ of that model, such that $c_xc_y = \pi_0^{E_0}u$; $\iota$ sends constants from $A\cap k_0$ to the corresponding constants; $\iota(c_x) = \gamma_U\cdot U$ and $\iota(c_y) = \gamma_V\cdot V$; $c_y$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$ and $c_x$ does not; $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\,q - a_0$ lies in $F_0$ and in $O$ and $\iota$ sends it to a unit multiple of $V^e$ with $e \ge 1$; there exists a valuation subring $W_x$ of $F_0$ containing $O$, over $A$, a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, containing an element $t$ such that a polynomial over $k_0$ with $A$-integral coefficients taking a value in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ at $t$ has all coefficients in the maximal ideal of $A\cap k_0$, with $c_x$ in and $c_y$ outside the maximal ideal of $W_x$, such that every $R_0$-integral $g$ of the level-$M'$ function field with poles only where $j$ has them lies in $F_0$ and in $W_x$, lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ precisely when its $R_0$-residue vanishes, and, when its $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, lies in $O$ and differs by a nonunit of $O$ from any constant $c \in k_0\cap A$ whose residue is the value of that residue at $s$; and such that every other node contains an element outside $W_x$; and there exists a subring $B_x$ of $F_0$ contained in $B \cap O$, whose elements have nonnegative order at every place of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ at which $j$ has nonnegative order, such that $O$ is the set of quotients $g/h$ with $g,h \in B_x$ and $h$ a unit of $O$, every element of $F_0$ is a quotient of elements of $B_x$ with nonzero denominator, $B_x$ is generated by the constants from $k_0\cap A$ together with a finite set, and some element of $B_x$ lies outside every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ which is over $A$, has $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal, contains $j$ with all monic $A$-integral polynomial values at $j$ units, and fails to contain some element of $O$.
--
--   This is the level-descent step in the construction of the semistable model of the modular curve at a supersingular point in residue characteristic $q = 3$, in the $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$ frame: the rigid chart data over the $k_0$-base change $K_\ell$ of the $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$-function field (an affine chart with a single supersingular closed point, its $q+1$ branch ends, the Drinfeld-curve reduction and the tame inertia law) are transported to the $k_0$-rational level field $F_0$ inside $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, producing there a discrete valuation ring $W_0$ over $A$, a smooth model $B$ over $A_b$ with Drinfeld reduction and inertia equivariance, and the $q+1$ nodes with their crossing models and Igusa separation. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_inertia_of_levelField_of_eq_three_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_inertia_of_levelField_of_eq_three_of_dvd).
